    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Inflation is broadly categorized into Demand-Pull and Cost-Push based on economic drivers.",
        "Speed-based inflation types range from Creeping and Walking to Galloping and Hyperinflation.",
        "Effects of inflation impact different socio-economic classes and broader macroeconomic growth differently.",
        "Effective control of inflation requires synchronized Monetary Measures by the RBI and Fiscal Measures by the Government."
